  "description": "The SCOTT Spark DC Factory takes everything we know about cross-country dominance and applies it to a design built for bigger trails. Engineered with greater suspension travel for harder-hitting terrain and paired with race-inspired performance, it's a platform purpose-built for deep missions into the mountain.\n\nEvery detail is considered to help you flow, climb, jump, and descend with equal confidence. A low center of mass creates a planted, controlled ride and a stable pedaling platform that keeps you grounded through the chaos—with no wasted energy. The lightweight, responsive feel comes courtesy of an HMX carbon frame engineered to make every gram count, delivering a ride worthy of the Spark legacy.\n\nThe suspension design draws directly from what we've learned at the World Cup level across both XC and Downhill. The result is a 140mm front and 138mm rear short-travel setup that refuses to be pigeonholed. RockShox's Pike trail fork and SIDLuxe XL shock—both with electronically controlled Ultimate Flight Attendant—adapt in real time to the terrain ahead, so you can open it up and ride without limits, knowing the ideal suspension setting is always dialed in.\n\nEquipped with SRAM's XX SL Eagle AXS Transmission drivetrain with power meter and Syncros Silverton CF1 wheels, the bike delivers a taste of World Cup racing performance on every trail you choose.\n\nIts capability extends well beyond setting a high pace. Generous mounting points support a full bikepacking setup for multi-day escapes, while integrated frame storage keeps your MTB essentials close—like our Save The Day kit. And when it's time for maintenance, suspension adjustments and component swaps are straightforward by design—so you can set the bike up exactly how you like it and get back on the trail with minimal interruption.\n\nThis is the evolution of the short-travel ripper—a bike that opens your riding to so much more than trail.\n\nPlease note that bike specifications are subject to change without prior notice.",
